(5668741, 824594, 30982, '<td valign="top">Post-voting comment upon request.  You got a 6 from me.  I thnk it meets the challenge, as it is indeed composed of straight lines and I do like that you''ve focused on the textures in the foreground yet still encompased the signs of decay in the background as well.  Where I think it is lacking a bit is the background, which predominates; it needs a focal point of sorts and less empty space.  As it is now, the pole with the round bit at the end dominates, and that fails to garner much interest in most viewers, I''d wager.  Maybe framing with more of the foreground, or getting up higher to look down more - get more of the door, less of the blown out sky?  I do like the "out of the box" type approach to this - I''m assuming that as you were shooting, you were considering ways for things to meet the challenge?  Gives you fun perspectives on things, even if the results don''t always give you good scores, yes?</td>', 'Post-voting comment upon request.  You got a 6 from me.  I thnk it meets the challenge, as it is indeed composed of straight lines and I do like that you''ve focused on the textures in the foreground yet still encompased the signs of decay in the background as well.  Where I think it is lacking a bit is the background, which predominates; it needs a focal point of sorts and less empty space.  As it is now, the pole with the round bit at the end dominates, and that fails to garner much interest in most viewers, I''d wager.  Maybe framing with more of the foreground, or getting up higher to look down more - get more of the door, less of the blown out sky?  I do like the "out of the box" type approach to this - I''m assuming that as you were shooting, you were considering ways for things to meet the challenge?  Gives you fun perspectives on things, even if the results don''t always give you good scores, yes?', '2009-10-01 02:46:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5668743, 823731, 30982, '<td valign="top">Post voting comment upon request.  I rather like these things as subject matter, but I''m weird.  Not everyone likes powerlines... go figure!  Anyway, meets the challenge - definitely lines, definitely straight.  Good color without being oversaturated (though oversaturated will often work well at DPC... use it sparingly).  Where it probably lacks in scoring is overall beyond-the-challenge "appeal" - in other words, it''s a solid shot, good focus, reasonably clean from noise, but is it something you''d use as a screensaver on your computer or print and hang by your desk?  Keep in mind that''s very subjective - many of my shots I can answer yes to those questions, but no one else would!  So you need to do two things, at a minimum, at DPC to score well - meet the challenge, unequivocably, and have appeal to the masses.</td>', 'Post voting comment upon request.  I rather like these things as subject matter, but I''m weird.  Not everyone likes powerlines... go figure!  Anyway, meets the challenge - definitely lines, definitely straight.  Good color without being oversaturated (though oversaturated will often work well at DPC... use it sparingly).  Where it probably lacks in scoring is overall beyond-the-challenge "appeal" - in other words, it''s a solid shot, good focus, reasonably clean from noise, but is it something you''d use as a screensaver on your computer or print and hang by your desk?  Keep in mind that''s very subjective - many of my shots I can answer yes to those questions, but no one else would!  So you need to do two things, at a minimum, at DPC to score well - meet the challenge, unequivocably, and have appeal to the masses.', '2009-10-01 02:51:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5668748, 823896, 64446, '<td valign="top">Love the repetition. The top left black steals a bit of it though. There are subtle non-straight lines there (the arches between columns) which might hit it hard scorewise.</td>', 'Love the repetition. The top left black steals a bit of it though. There are subtle non-straight lines there (the arches between columns) which might hit it hard scorewise.', '2009-10-01 02:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
