(5681276, 824547, 90495, '<td valign="top">Is this a macro of a dollhouse? lol I didn''t think this was you Irene when I first laid eyes on it. Beautiful hallway and you captured its beauty splendidly. B&amp;W was well suited for this too. The washed out doorway at the end gives this shot an eerie feeling, once you notice it. It makes me think of the movie The Shining for some reason. ''gratz</td>', 'Is this a macro of a dollhouse? lol I didn''t think this was you Irene when I first laid eyes on it. Beautiful hallway and you captured its beauty splendidly. B&W was well suited for this too. The washed out doorway at the end gives this shot an eerie feeling, once you notice it. It makes me think of the movie The Shining for some reason. ''gratz', '2009-10-09 00:24:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5681279, 823882, 90495, '<td valign="top">Very well captured. I like this type of architectural photography. ''gratz on a top 5 finish.</td>', 'Very well captured. I like this type of architectural photography. ''gratz on a top 5 finish.', '2009-10-09 00:27:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5681287, 823534, 82112, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Magnum_za:</b></div><hr/><i> I loved this, made me wonder who (or what) I''m sharing the cage with! Would have liked to see what it was I''m being fed...8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Breadcrumbs, Italian Style. Very tasty.<br/>Thanks for the engaging comment.<br/> <br/>-Essay</td>', 'Originally posted by Magnum_za: I loved this, made me wonder who (or what) I''m sharing the cage with! Would have liked to see what it was I''m being fed...8   Breadcrumbs, Italian Style. Very tasty.Thanks for the engaging comment. -Essay', '2009-10-09 00:38:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5681730, 824411, 96227, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the window reflection...I took this shot from inside a moving train in burst mode to try and catch the bridge on the inside.  Since there is no editing in this challenge I could not clone out the reflections.</td>', 'Sorry about the window reflection...I took this shot from inside a moving train in burst mode to try and catch the bridge on the inside.  Since there is no editing in this challenge I could not clone out the reflections.', '2009-10-09 13:53:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5682492, 824681, 68956, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Well, there''s not a lot to not like about this image and your score and placement reflect that!<br/>The composition is very strong and the b&amp;w conversion is excellent. The one thing that detracts from the image, for me, is the border. I checked that I actually did prefer it without the border by cropping it off and I preferred the resulting image. But that is a minor detail and very subjective!<br/>Overall an excellent image and one to be proud of :)</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club! Well, there''s not a lot to not like about this image and your score and placement reflect that!The composition is very strong and the b&w conversion is excellent. The one thing that detracts from the image, for me, is the border. I checked that I actually did prefer it without the border by cropping it off and I preferred the resulting image. But that is a minor detail and very subjective!Overall an excellent image and one to be proud of :)', '2009-10-10 09:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5682647, 824664, 100831, '<td valign="top">terrific shot! Great pov and colors. Congratulations!!</td>', 'terrific shot! Great pov and colors. Congratulations!!', '2009-10-10 13:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5683653, 823349, 27845, '<td valign="top">Heh, good thing the Philharmonie hasn''t been overdone on this website yet. Just visiting Luxembourg or resident photographer?</td>', 'Heh, good thing the Philharmonie hasn''t been overdone on this website yet. Just visiting Luxembourg or resident photographer?', '2009-10-11 17:47:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5684672, 824601, 68956, '<td valign="top">Hi Dale from the Critique Club!<br/>I love the colours and lighting in your image, very rich and seductive. I usually like a shallow DOF but I don''t feel it works well in this picture, the point (excuse the pun ;) ) of focus is at the very edge of the frame and my eye spends most of it''s time elsewhere and there''s nothing comfortable to rest my eyes on. The double reflection makes me feel a bit funny too, as though I''m going cross-eyed. A cleaner reflection, a larger DOF and a different placement of point of focus might turn this from a good image into a stunning one!<br/> <br/>I hope that doesn''t sound too negative, I really enjoyed spending time with your image :)</td>', 'Hi Dale from the Critique Club!I love the colours and lighting in your image, very rich and seductive. I usually like a shallow DOF but I don''t feel it works well in this picture, the point (excuse the pun ;) ) of focus is at the very edge of the frame and my eye spends most of it''s time elsewhere and there''s nothing comfortable to rest my eyes on. The double reflection makes me feel a bit funny too, as though I''m going cross-eyed. A cleaner reflection, a larger DOF and a different placement of point of focus might turn this from a good image into a stunning one! I hope that doesn''t sound too negative, I really enjoyed spending time with your image :)', '2009-10-12 16:53:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5684686, 823349, 106820, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gloda:</b></div><hr/><i> Heh, good thing the Philharmonie hasn''t been overdone on this website yet. Just visiting Luxembourg or resident photographer? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-16 02:34:30.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by gloda: Heh, good thing the Philharmonie hasn''t been overdone on this website yet. Just visiting Luxembourg or resident photographer?   ', '2009-10-12 17:09:39.000000', '2010-02-16 02:34:30.000000', 0),
(5684702, 824664, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wow - just noticed this was a new personal best for you - congratulations!!  This was one of my top choices for the challenge - really pleased to see this did so well.</td>', 'Wow - just noticed this was a new personal best for you - congratulations!!  This was one of my top choices for the challenge - really pleased to see this did so well.', '2009-10-12 17:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5685108, 824601, 110294, '<td valign="top">Thank you so much Critique Club. I want to thank you for giving me your feedback. It is very much appreciated and I am thankful that there are people willing to help me and my photography.<br/> <br/>Have an awesome week.<br/>Dale</td>', 'Thank you so much Critique Club. I want to thank you for giving me your feedback. It is very much appreciated and I am thankful that there are people willing to help me and my photography. Have an awesome week.Dale', '2009-10-12 22:27:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5685110, 824601, 110294, '<td valign="top">I would also like to thank everyone for your votes and comments, this was a fun challenge and look forward to even more.<br/>Dale</td>', 'I would also like to thank everyone for your votes and comments, this was a fun challenge and look forward to even more.Dale', '2009-10-12 22:27:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5685299, 823882, 24486, '<td valign="top">Pam, congratulations on 4th place &amp; a new PB. Excellant choice with the B&amp;W.</td>', 'Pam, congratulations on 4th place & a new PB. Excellant choice with the B&W.', '2009-10-13 06:36:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5685903, 823349, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fshiis:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you all for your comment.<br/>I hoped to get in the top 20 and I get the 2nd place. I am very very happy. Especially because I have (only) a ixus 860 and when I see the pictures of all these competitions, we dare not participate. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nowadays in here, it seems that the camera isn''t as important as what you can do with the editing of a shot. :)  If you get a decent enough photo and can do some decent editing, you don''t need a full geared DSLR camera!  :)  You''ve just proven that!!! :)</td>', 'Originally posted by fshiis: Thank you all for your comment.I hoped to get in the top 20 and I get the 2nd place. I am very very happy. Especially because I have (only) a ixus 860 and when I see the pictures of all these competitions, we dare not participate.   Nowadays in here, it seems that the camera isn''t as important as what you can do with the editing of a shot. :)  If you get a decent enough photo and can do some decent editing, you don''t need a full geared DSLR camera!  :)  You''ve just proven that!!! :)', '2009-10-13 20:43:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5690192, 824689, 108580, '<td valign="top">Nice use of angles and lines Dan. Also odd that there are no boats docked at all?<br/>If you did 1/80th handheld well done. I battle and use a tripod nowadays.<br/> <br/>Did you try taking a few shots at exactly the same spot? i.e. gone low and made the poles look like giants reaching to the sky, this would have lost thier reflection in the water. Gone potrait and landscape. Fiddled with the camera settings and tried Sunlight, Shade, Sport, Building etc to see what came out?<br/> <br/>Damn that place looks cold and wet.<br/></td>', 'Nice use of angles and lines Dan. Also odd that there are no boats docked at all?If you did 1/80th handheld well done. I battle and use a tripod nowadays. Did you try taking a few shots at exactly the same spot? i.e. gone low and made the poles look like giants reaching to the sky, this would have lost thier reflection in the water. Gone potrait and landscape. Fiddled with the camera settings and tried Sunlight, Shade, Sport, Building etc to see what came out? Damn that place looks cold and wet.', '2009-10-17 01:52:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5692636, 824331, 66267, '<td valign="top">i find the awseomness of this shot a bit distracting<br/> <br/>i rate it a jon</td>', 'i find the awseomness of this shot a bit distracting i rate it a jon', '2009-10-19 17:59:06.000000', NULL, 0),
